Backend Created with Lifetime In-memory <code>InstanceConfig::memory()</code> / <code>new Instance('{}')</code> Lost when the handle closes Directory <code>{"data_dir": "..."}</code> config Persisted by the fjall backend <p>A directory instance takes an exclusive <code>LOCK</code> file. One process may open it; a second opener fails instead of corrupting data. In-memory instances have no such restriction — open as many as the process needs.</p> RustTypeScriptPython <pre><code>use datastreamdb_core::{Instance, InstanceConfig};

let scratch = Instance::open(InstanceConfig::memory())?;
let durable = Instance::open(InstanceConfig::from_json(
    r#"{"data_dir": "./data/app", "tenant": "app"}"#,
)?)?;
</code></pre> <pre><code>import { Instance } from '@datastreamdb/core'

const scratch = new Instance('{}')
const durable = new Instance(JSON.stringify({ data_dir: './data/app' }))
</code></pre> <pre><code>from datastreamdb import Instance

scratch = Instance("{}")
durable = Instance('{"data_dir": "./data/app"}')
</code></pre>

